---
import SightlineLayout from "@/layouts/SightlineLayout.astro";
---

<SightlineLayout
  title="About — Sightline"
  description="How Sightline connects photographs to places, and what its reconstructions can tell us."
>
  <article class="about-page sightline-shell">
    <header class="sightline-page-head">
      <h1>Behind the view.</h1>
      <p>Sightline brings photographs back to the places they were taken.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="method-copy">
      <h2>From a photograph to a viewpoint</h2>
      <p>
        Location data and visual matches help estimate the camera’s position and
        direction. In supported cities, you can explore that viewpoint in 3D and
        compare it with the photograph.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="method-copy">
      <h2>A result is not a guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        Accepted, rejected, approximate, and missing results stay distinct. A
        solved camera still needs verification and publication approval. GPS
        uncertainty, changed scenery, and incomplete 3D coverage can affect
        alignment.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="method-copy">
      <h2>Only reviewed records are public</h2>
      <p>
        This collection uses reviewed photographs and location records. Original
        files and private metadata stay offline. Map imagery comes directly from
        its provider, with attribution.
      </p>
    </section>
    <a class="sightline-text-link" href="/"
      >Back to the collection <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    >
  </article>
</SightlineLayout>
